---
// A banner for posts an LLM drafted. Some posts here are written by a model
// working from my notes, my measurements and a lot of me complaining at the
// screen. That is worth saying out loud rather than letting a reader work it
// out from the prose, so this sits at the top of those posts.
//
// Pass children to override the wording for a specific post.
---

<aside class="llm-disclaimer">
  <p class="label">Written by a machine</p>
  <slot>
    <p>
      An LLM wrote this post. I shouted at my screen for an afternoon, pointed
      it at the changelog, made it measure things until the numbers were honest,
      and this came out. I checked the facts and every command in here is real
      output. I did not rewrite the prose. So if a sentence reads a little off,
      that is why.
    </p>
  </slot>
</aside>

<style>
  .llm-disclaimer {
    border-left: 4px solid var(--teal-500);
    background-color: var(--teal-50);
    padding: var(--spacing-300) var(--spacing-400);
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-600);
    border-radius: 0 var(--radius) var(--radius) 0;
  }

  .label {
    color: var(--teal-700);
    font-size: var(--font-300);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: var(--spacing-100);
  }

  /* The post stylesheet gives every paragraph a bottom margin, which leaves a
     gap under the last line of the banner. The banner sets its own spacing. */
  .llm-disclaimer :global(p) {
    font-size: var(--font-400);
    font-weight: 300;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .llm-disclaimer :global(p + p) {
    margin-top: var(--spacing-200);
  }
</style>
